<span class=\"ltx_contact ltx_role_email\"><span class=\"ltx_contact_name\">email: </span><a href=\"mailto:wei.ji@yale.edu\">wei.ji@yale.edu</a>\n</span></span></span></span>\n<span class=\"ltx_author_before\">, </span><span class=\"ltx_creator ltx_role_author\">\n<span class=\"ltx_personname\">Jingjing Li\n</span><span class=\"ltx_author_notes\"><span class=\"ltx_author_notes_content\">\n<span class=\"ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation\"><span class=\"ltx_contact_name\">Affiliation: </span><span id=\"id16\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_affiliation_institution\">Carnegie Mellon University</span>\n, <span id=\"id17\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_affiliation_city\">Pittsburgh</span>\n, <span id=\"id18\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_affiliation_country\">United States</span>\n</span>\n<span class=\"ltx_contact ltx_role_email\"><span class=\"ltx_contact_name\">email: </span><a href=\"mailto:jingjingli.cmu@gmail.com\">jingjingli.cmu@gmail.com</a>\n</span></span></span></span>\n<span class=\"ltx_author_before\">, </span><span class=\"ltx_creator ltx_role_author\">\n<span class=\"ltx_personname\">Yongri Piao\n</span><span class=\"ltx_author_notes\"><span class=\"ltx_author_notes_content\">\n<span class=\"ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation\"><span class=\"ltx_contact_name\">Affiliation: </span><span id=\"id19\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_affiliation_institution\">Dalian University of Technology</span>\n, <span id=\"id20\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_affiliation_city\">Dalian</span>\n, <span id=\"id21\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_affiliation_country\">China</span>\n</span>\n<span class=\"ltx_contact ltx_role_email\"><span class=\"ltx_contact_name\">email: </span><a href=\"mailto:yrpiao@dlut.edu.cn\">yrpiao@dlut.edu.cn</a>\n</span></span></span></span>\n<span class=\"ltx_author_before\"> and </span><span class=\"ltx_creator ltx_role_author\">\n<span class=\"ltx_personname\">Huchuan Lu\n</span><span class=\"ltx_author_notes\"><span class=\"ltx_author_notes_content\">\n<span class=\"ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation\"><span class=\"ltx_contact_name\">Affiliation: </span><span id=\"id22\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_affiliation_institution\">Dalian University of Technology</span>\n, <span id=\"id23\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_affiliation_city\">Dalian</span>\n, <span id=\"id24\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_affiliation_country\">China</span>\n</span>\n<span class=\"ltx_contact ltx_role_email\"><span class=\"ltx_contact_name\">email: </span><a href=\"mailto:lhchuan@dlut.edu.cn\">lhchuan@dlut.edu.cn</a>\n</span></span></span></span></div>\n<div class=\"ltx_dates\">2026; © cc</div>\n\n<div id=\"abstract1\" class=\"ltx_abstract\"><h6 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_abstract\">Abstract.</h6>\n    \n<p id=\"abstract1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">Audio-Visual Instance Segmentation (AVIS) aims to simultaneously classify, segment, and track sounding objects within video sequences. Unlike Audio-Visual Semantic Segmentation (AVS), AVIS involves instance-level modeling across longer video sequences, introducing two key challenges: (1) complex modality-state changes disrupt long-range modeling, and (2) substantial structural and distributional discrepancies between modalities hinder precise instance-level association. Existing methods rely on fixed-step Transformers and recursive Mamba models, lacking adaptability to modality-state changes. In addition, methods performing implicit matching ignore the inherent distributional inconsistencies. To address these issues, we propose a framework with Adaptive Dynamic Step Modulation (ADSM) and Optimal Transport-based Matching Modulation (OT-MM). ADSM adaptively modulates Mamba step sizes using temporal variation, cross-modal discrepancy, and historical context, balancing rapid response to modality-state changes with stable long-range modeling. OT-MM explicitly formulates instance-level cross-modal matching as an entropy-regularized optimal transport problem solved via log-domain Sinkhorn iterations, and further enforces distribution-level coherence with an MMD regularizer. Extensive experiments demonstrate state-of-the-art performance on the AVIS benchmark (+3.76 FSLA, +2.75 HOTA, +2.58 mAP), verified through comprehensive qualitative visualizations. <span id=\"abstract1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_italic\">The code and model are available at <a href=\"https://github.com/happylife-pk/SAMOT\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter\">https://github.com/happylife-pk/SAMOT</a>.</span></p>\n  \n</div>\n<div class=\"ltx_keywords\">\n<h6 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_keywords\">Keywords: </h6>Audio-Visual Instance Segmentation, Multimodal Fusion,\nState Space Model, Optimal Transport\n</div><span id=\"id25\" class=\"ltx_note ltx_role_cc-license\"><sup class=\"ltx_note_mark\">†</sup><span class=\"ltx_note_outer\"><span class=\"ltx_note_content\"><sup class=\"ltx_note_mark\">†</sup><span class=\"ltx_note_type\">cc-license: </span>by</span></span></span>\n<figure id=\"S0.F1\" class=\"ltx_figure\"><img src=\"2608.08147v1/motivation.png\" id=\"S0.F1.g1\" class=\"ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape\" width=\"476\" height=\"203\" alt=\"Refer to caption\">\n<figcaption class=\"ltx_caption ltx_centering\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure\">Figure 1. </span>Illustration of the two core challenges in AVIS. (a) Although the visual content remains stable, the active sources are the dog at T1, both the person and the dog at T2, and the person\nat T3. These modality-state changes disrupt stable long-range modeling. (b) Structural and distributional discrepancies between audio and visual modalities hinder precise instance-level correspondence.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<section id=\"S1\" class=\"ltx_section\">\n<h2 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_section\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_section\">1. </span>Introduction</h2>\n\n<div id=\"S1.p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n<p id=\"S1.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">Audio-Visual Instance Segmentation (AVIS) <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep\">(<a href=\"#bib.bib20\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">Guo et al. 2025</a>)</cite> is a novel task designed to s", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false, "persistedOutputPath": "/inspire/qb-ilm/project/video-generation/chenxie-25019/hyr/iHateTheWorld555.github.io/.claude-review/projects/-inspire-qb-ilm-project-video-generation-chenxie-25019-hyr-iHateTheWorld555-github-io/659aad1a-e56a-4dba-b885-840ed5aa12b3/tool-results/bi5vkfhgh.txt", "persistedOutputSize": 234220}}
