{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-99ab1a59af1d490e", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# MambaVoiceCloning: Efficient and Expressive Text-to-Speech via State-Space Modeling and Diffusion Control\narXiv: 2604.00292\nAuthors: Sahil Kumar, Namrataben Patel, Honggang Wang, Youshan Zhang\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A diffusion-based TTS system with a fully SSM-only inference-time conditioning path spanning text, rhythm, and prosody under a fixed decoder.\n  2. A gated bidirectional Mamba fusion with AdaLN that improves long-range prosody stability and reduces drift on multi-sentence and out-of-distribution text.\n  3. Protocol- and capacity-matched baselines that isolate the architectural impact of removing inference-time attention.\n  4. A deployment-oriented analysis covering memory usage, throughput, SSM hyperparameter sensitivity, long-form behavior, and finite look-ahead streaming, demonstrating predictable linear-time characteristics.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-流式", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "659aad1a-e56a-4dba-b885-840ed5aa12b3", "uuid": "98195613-08bb-44ef-b56f-fc8dd44a7cd9", "timestamp": "2026-08-12T03:46:09.057Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# MambaVoiceCloning: Efficient and Expressive Text-to-Speech via State-Space Modeling and Diffusion Control\narXiv: 2604.00292\nAuthors: Sahil Kumar, Namrataben Patel, Honggang Wang, Youshan Zhang\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A diffusion-based TTS system with a fully SSM-only inference-time conditioning path spanning text, rhythm, and prosody under a fixed decoder.\n  2. A gated bidirectional Mamba fusion with AdaLN that improves long-range prosody stability and reduces drift on multi-sentence and out-of-distribution text.\n  3. Protocol- and capacity-matched baselines that isolate the architectural impact of removing inference-time attention.\n  4. A deployment-oriented analysis covering memory usage, throughput, SSM hyperparameter sensitivity, long-form behavior, and finite look-ahead streaming, demonstrating predictable linear-time characteristics.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-流式", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a812c6c9941d9f42", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# AISHELL6-whisper: A Chinese Mandarin Audio-visual Whisper Speech Dataset with Speech Recognition Baselines\narXiv: 2509.23833\nAuthors: Cancan Li, Fei Su, Juan Liu, Hui Bu, Yulong Wan, Hongbin Suo, Ming Li\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_dataset\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We present AISHELL6-Whisper, the largest open-source Chinese Mandarin audio-visual whisper speech dataset featuring 30 hours each of parallel whisper and normal speech with synchronized frontal facial videos.\n  2. We propose an audio-visual speech recognition baseline based on the Whisper-Flamingo framework that integrates a parallel training strategy to align embeddings across speech types.\n  3. We introduce a lightweight projection layer specifically designed to adapt the model to whisper speech's spectral properties and bridge the acoustic gap with normal speech.\n  4. Our proposed model achieves a Character Error Rate of 4.13% for whisper speech and 1.11% for normal speech on the AISHELL6-Whisper test set.\n  5. Our approach establishes new state-of-the-art results on the public wTIMIT benchmark, demonstrating strong cross-lingual transferability.\n\nTags: ASR, ASR/训练-SSL微调, ASR/训练-监督", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "659aad1a-e56a-4dba-b885-840ed5aa12b3", "uuid": "a065d1b8-a75f-4ea8-8ba6-5a99151297ef", "timestamp": "2026-08-12T03:46:09.304Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# AISHELL6-whisper: A Chinese Mandarin Audio-visual Whisper Speech Dataset with Speech Recognition Baselines\narXiv: 2509.23833\nAuthors: Cancan Li, Fei Su, Juan Liu, Hui Bu, Yulong Wan, Hongbin Suo, Ming Li\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_dataset\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We present AISHELL6-Whisper, the largest open-source Chinese Mandarin audio-visual whisper speech dataset featuring 30 hours each of parallel whisper and normal speech with synchronized frontal facial videos.\n  2. We propose an audio-visual speech recognition baseline based on the Whisper-Flamingo framework that integrates a parallel training strategy to align embeddings across speech types.\n  3. We introduce a lightweight projection layer specifically designed to adapt the model to whisper speech's spectral properties and bridge the acoustic gap with normal speech.\n  4. Our proposed model achieves a Character Error Rate of 4.13% for whisper speech and 1.11% for normal speech on the AISHELL6-Whisper test set.\n  5. Our approach establishes new state-of-the-art results on the public wTIMIT benchmark, demonstrating strong cross-lingual transferability.\n\nTags: ASR, ASR/训练-SSL微调, ASR/训练-监督", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-99afe408d92ef472", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Adversarial Flow Models\narXiv: 2511.22475\nAuthors: Shanchuan Lin, Ceyuan Yang, Zhijie Lin, Hao Chen, Haoqi Fan\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_other\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. The paper introduces adversarial flow models, a hybrid generative model class belonging to both the adversarial and flow families that supports native single-step and multi-step generation.\n  2. The method stabilizes adversarial training by constraining the generator to learn a deterministic optimal transport map via a novel optimal transport regularization loss, preventing the generator drift common in standard GANs.\n  3. Unlike consistency-based methods, the model directly learns one-step or few-step generation without consuming capacity on intermediate probability flow timesteps, thereby avoiding error accumulation.\n  4. The approach generalizes to discrete-time flow modeling by incorporating flow-matching interpolation functions, allowing transport between arbitrary timesteps along the probability flow.\n  5. A gradient-normalization technique is proposed to decouple the varying magnitude of discriminator gradients from the optimal transport loss, enabling a single hyperparameter to work across different model sizes.\n  6. A flow-based classifier guidance method is introduced to incorporate accumulated guidance gradients along the probability flow, successfully adapting classifier-free guidance behavior to single-step adversarial models.\n  7. The method enables stable end-to-end training of extra-deep transformers (up to 112 layers) using block repetition without any intermediate supervision, demonstrating that single-step generation quality can scale with model depth.\n  8. The proposed models achieve state-of-the-art FID scores on ImageNet-256px, including a 1NFE FID of 2.38 with the XL/2 model and a 1NFE FID of 1.94 with 